title:    Both paths work, from a VM with no external IP
subtitle: Same API, same machine - only the address curl connects to differs
width:    980
---
baseline: Private Google Access -> 401   PSC endpoint -> 401

# 401 is the proof, not a problem. The call reached Google and was refused for
# lack of credentials, which means the network path completed. A path that does
# not work returns 000: the connection never opened at all.
#
# PGA  curl https://storage.googleapis.com         (default DNS -> a Google VIP)
# PSC  curl --resolve storage.googleapis.com:443:10.99.0.2
#
# The VM has no external IP and there is no Cloud NAT on this network, so
# neither of these is an ordinary internet call.
